  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Berry cobbler is a generous, informal pudding, sharp berries in a jammy sauce, a golden dropped-scone crust, and very little effort beyond mixing two separate bowls and combining them in a dish. The berries cook down rapidly and their juices thicken under the topping, so the sauce around each serving is deep red and intense. Frozen berries work excellently here and need no thawing before use. Bake at 190°C for 30 to 35 minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
